course: dictionary
lesson: 8365
title: Roughly: about, not exactly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Roughly» means about, not exactly. When you say roughly 100 people came, you are giving a close guess, not an exact count.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Children have 20 milk teeth, which fall out roughly from age 6 to 12.» Children do not all lose a tooth at the same age, so roughly tells you the ages are close, not exact.
explain: «Roughly» can also mean not gentle, as in «He pushed me roughly», or not neat, as in «roughly cut pieces». Check your meaning by swapping it in: does about, or not gentle, or not neat, still make sense?
fact: Roughly means about, not exactly: roughly 100 people means close to 100, perhaps 98 or 103.
fact: «The inner core is roughly as hot as the surface of the Sun», so its heat is close to the Sun's, about 5,000-6,000 °C.
fact: In maths, roughly signals an estimate: 398 + 205 is roughly 400 + 200 = 600.
fact: Roughly can also mean not gently or not carefully, as in «He pushed me roughly» or «roughly cut pieces».
fact: Useful phrases: roughly speaking, roughly the same, roughly equal.
exercise: «Children have 20 milk teeth, which fall out roughly from age 6 to 12.» What does roughly mean here? | Never | *About, not exact | Exactly on the day | Very gently
exercise: «He pushed me roughly out of the way.» What does roughly mean here? | Exactly | Very carefully | Quietly | *Not gently
exercise: Ella says, «The shop had roughly 50 apples.» What does roughly tell us? | Fewer than 5 apples | Only red apples | *Close to 50, not exactly 50 | Exactly 50 apples
test: Which sentence uses roughly to mean not neatly? | She ate the sandwich slowly | *The pieces of wood were roughly cut | The bus was on time
test: In maths, 398 + 205 is roughly what? | 603 | 6000 | *600 | 500
exam: Which word best replaces roughly in «roughly 100 people came»? | *About | Never | Exactly | Quickly
